{"type":"text","text":"Done. Both origins are found, proven, and recorded.\n\n## Results\n\n**1. ? block 16x16 tile-id table — prgRom `0xC8C` (CPU `$8C8C`)**\n- 4 bytes, column-major: `53 55 54 56` = [top-left, bottom-left, top-right, bottom-right]. The nametable gets `$53/$54` on the top row and `$55/$56` on the bottom row.\n- It is one entry of a 4-byte-per-entry block table running `0xC84–0xCA3` (`B0 B1 B2 B3 / 77 79 77 79 / 53 55 54 56 / 53 55 54 56 / A5 A7 A6 A8 / C2 C4 C3 C5 / 57 59 58 5A / 7B 7D 7C 7E`). The identical entry at `0xC90` is *not* the one World 1-1's ? blocks use.\n- **Proof:** wrote `$53 → $00` (ledger seq 1), reset, replayed to 1-1. `get_tile_at_pixel` on the floating block's top-left then returned tile_id 0 (palette 3, chr_tile `$100` = HUD \"0\" glyph) while the other three quadrants stayed `$54/$55/$56`; the screenshot showed a \"0\" in the top-left of every ? block on screen. `undo_edit` restored `$53`.\n\n**2. small Mario standing-frame tile table — prgRom `0x6ED3` (CPU `$EED3`)**\n- 4 bytes `3A 37 4F 4F`, the read of an 8-byte player-graphics record `FC FC FC FC 3A 37 4F 4F` (the leading `$FC`s pad small Mario into the 2×4 big-Mario OAM box). Neighbouring records are other poses (`0x6E8B` = `3A 37 3B 3C`, `0x6EC3` = `3A 37 92 93`).\n- **Proof:** wrote `$3A → $FC` (ledger seq 1), reset. `list_sprites` then returned chr_tile 252 (blank, `opaque:false`) for the top-left cell at (40,193) that had read 58 (`$3A`); `get_pixel_color(45,196)` read hill green `$1A` where the old tile had content, while (48,196) still read Mario skin `$27`. `undo_edit` restored `$3A`.\n\n## Session bookkeeping\n- `new_hack eval-sheet2-tiles` + `use_hack` done before any ROM write; both edits ledgered there and both undone, so its ledger is empty.\n- `record_mapping` ×2 (a `note` at `0xC8C`, a `sprite` `mario_small_standing` at `0x6ED3`, both `source: \"search and ledgered write\"`, `confidence: 1`, with `rom_origins` and the proof in `notes`), then `promote_mappings` (2 discoveries promoted).\n- `use_hack default` restored at the end; emulator left paused (World 1-1, title/level state as the replay left it).\n\nMethod note: the ? block tiles were only findable by `search_memory` because they are stored **column-major** — the row-major run `53 54 55 56` does not exist in PRG."}
